method:
Only aggregate numbers leave this script; no performance is copied.  Method:
- 4/4 performances labelled 'beat'; the drum notes grouped as the paper's simplified mapping groups them, with the
  cross-stick, the hi-hat pedal and the ride bell kept apart (they are separate sounds in the blocks);
- each performance is called swung when more of its cymbal and snare onsets fall nearest a triplet position of the
  beat than nearest a sixteenth position (other than the beat itself); straight performances are read on a grid of
  sixteenths, swung ones on a grid of triplet eighths;
- the files begin where the recording began, which is a bar line for most: a performance whose kicks and crashes both
  fall more often on beat 3 than on beat 1 is read from half a bar later, as having started mid-bar (the kick enters
  on the downbeat, and a crash marks the downbeat after a fill: Open Music Theory, "Drumbeats");
- a fill is where the hands leave the cymbals (closed or open hi-hat, ride) from a beat to the end of the bar while
  the snare or toms play at least twice there, as Open Music Theory's "Drumbeats" describes a fill (the cymbals stop);
- a feel (the drummer's primary style label) is kept when it has at least MIN_BARS bars from at least two drummers,
  none of whom played more than MAX_ONE_DRUMMER of them, so that no feel is one drummer's habits.
